<title>MALAYSIA: Country Heights falls on requotation.</title>
<headline>Country Heights falls on requotation.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Malaysia's Country Heights Holdings Bhd fell on requotation following its announcement of a planned 3-for-5 bonus issue.</p>
<p>Around 0208 GMT, the stock was down 2.0 ringgit or 11.17 percent to 15.90 on volume of 278,000 shares traded.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the stock had a good run-up in recent weeks on expectations the company would benefit from projects linked to Malaysia's new administrative capital of Putrajaya.</p>
<p>The stock was suspended on May 26.</p>
<p>&quot;It's normal for the Malaysian market, to sell on announcement after buying on rumours,&quot; said an Arab-Malaysian Securities institutional dealer.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
